Title: Agent Credential Management
Shortname: agent-credential-management
Level: 1
Status: DREAM
Text Macro: LONGSTATUS Independent Discussion Draft (v0)
Editor: Nick Steele, OpenAI
Date: 2026-10-14
Abstract: This discussion draft proposes a provider-neutral interface for software agents to request use of managed credentials. A credential manager keeps credentials by default, applies policy and any required user verification, and performs operations for approved destinations. A trusted runtime authenticates the requester and supplies execution context; agents work with opaque references. This v0 explains why that separation is useful, how a request is processed, and what the public interface looks like through minimal IDL and worked examples. It is not an implementation commitment or a complete wire protocol.
